The intended behavior:
- debounce(fn, waitMs) returns a function that delays calling fn until waitMs milliseconds have passed since the LAST call
- Passes through the latest arguments
- Cancels any pending call when a new one arrives

So when you call the returned function:
1. If there's a pending timer, cancel it first (clearTimeout)
2. Schedule a new timer for waitMs ms
